Apply to `ash_authentication` on its 5.x line, before this package releases.

The password sign in form hands its sign in token to the `sign_in_with_token`
route in a POST body instead of a query string. That route declares GET only, so
`AshAuthentication.Phoenix.StrategyRouter` rejects the POST until this lands.

POST is added alongside GET, so GET keeps working. `StrategyRouter` already wraps
the result of `method_for_phase/2` in a list, and `OAuth2` already returns
`[:get, :post]` for its `:callback` phase, so the list shape is not new.

This package cannot release its side until an `ash_authentication` version that
carries this change is on Hex, and its dependency floor moves to that version.

Apply with:

    git apply /path/to/ash-authentication-main.patch

diff --git a/lib/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy.ex b/lib/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy.ex
index b55c1ba..339c025 100644
--- a/lib/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy.ex
+++ b/lib/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy.ex
@@ -46,8 +46,8 @@ defimpl AshAuthentication.Strategy, for: AshAuthentication.Strategy.Password do
   def actions(strategy), do: phases(strategy)
 
   @doc false
-  @spec method_for_phase(Password.t(), phase) :: Strategy.http_method()
-  def method_for_phase(_, phase) when phase in [:sign_in_with_token], do: :get
+  @spec method_for_phase(Password.t(), phase) :: Strategy.http_method() | [Strategy.http_method()]
+  def method_for_phase(_, phase) when phase in [:sign_in_with_token], do: [:get, :post]
   def method_for_phase(_, _), do: :post
 
   @doc """
diff --git a/test/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy_test.exs b/test/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy_test.exs
index 0b94ea4..7581d29 100644
--- a/test/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy_test.exs
+++ b/test/ash_authentication/strategies/password/strategy_test.exs
@@ -74,8 +74,8 @@ defmodule AshAuthentication.Strategy.Password.StrategyTest do
     end
 
     for phase <- ~w[sign_in_with_token]a do
-      test "it is get for the #{phase} phase" do
-        assert :get ==
+      test "it accepts both get and post for the #{phase} phase" do
+        assert [:get, :post] ==
                  %Password{}
                  |> Strategy.method_for_phase(unquote(phase))
       end
